   "title": "How this works",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Video review\nFour independent samples: first frame, one third, two thirds, last frame. Start and end requirements include their states; middle requirements include unchanged facts and allowed cast counts. All four reviews must pass. Sampling is not a guarantee about unsampled frames. The studio blocks a new final cut when any clip lacks a current passing review.\n\nAI mode: Normal uses Gemma 4 12B at 8-bit; Fast uses E4B. Change the Open Cinema Writer mode widget. Image and video models stay the same. Cast-review findings retain the saved candidate; inspect it before using it downstream."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
